<title>FRANCE: Elf 96 pre-except net income 7.52 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Elf 96 pre-except net income 7.52 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable excl special items  7,518  vs	   5,325</p>
<p>    Net attributable			   6,977  vs	   5,035</p>
<p>    Operating				   21,725  vs	  15,487</p>
<p>    Sales					232,707  vs	 208,290</p>
<p>    Operating before special items	22,266  vs	  15,487</p>
<p>    -- exploration and production	 15,735  vs	   8,008</p>
<p>    -- refining &amp; marketing, trading	 447  vs		 4</p>
<p>    -- chemicals				 3,645  vs	   4,959</p>
<p>-- health 2,458 vs 2,489</p>
<p>    Consolidated net income		  6,977  vs	   5,035</p>
<p>    Net income excluding special items   7,518  vs	   5,325</p>
<p>    Funds generated from operations     31,139  vs	  28,626</p>
<p>    Investments (excl. exploration)     28,312  vs	  29,574</p>
<p>    Proceeds from the sale of assets     7,655  vs	   8,191</p>
<p>    net debt to equity ratio (pct)	    37  vs		38</p>
<p>    net dividend (francs)			 14  vs		13</p>
<p>    net income per share (francs)	     28  vs		20</p>
<p>NOTE - Elf Aquitaine gave the figures in a statement. Analysts had been expecting an income per share figure of about 27.7 francs. Elf had said in December it expected net income to be between 7.3 and 7.5 billion francs.</p>
</text>
